# Node.js + TypeScript Project Standards

## Purpose
Enforce consistent file, folder, and naming conventions across the backend codebase.

This project follows a feature-first modular architecture using strict naming conventions.

---

# 1. Folder Structure Standard

## Required Structure

All domain logic must be organized by feature/module:

src/
  modules/
    <feature-name>/
      <feature>-controller.ts
      <feature>-service.ts
      <feature>-repository.ts
      <feature>.types.ts
      <feature>.interface.ts
      create-<feature>.dto.ts
      update-<feature>.dto.ts
      <feature>-validator.ts

Do NOT use layer-first global folders like:
- controllers/
- services/
- repositories/

Feature-based modular structure is mandatory.

---

# 2. Folder Naming Rules

- Must use kebab-case
- Must be lowercase
- No underscores
- No PascalCase

✅ user-profile
❌ UserProfile
❌ user_profile

---

# 3. File Naming Rules

All files must:

- Use kebab-case
- Be lowercase
- Include role suffix when applicable
- Be descriptive and explicit

Examples:

user-controller.ts
auth-service.ts
order-repository.ts
jwt-middleware.ts
create-user.dto.ts
user.types.ts
user.interface.ts
user-service.spec.ts

Forbidden patterns:

UserController.ts
userController.ts
user_controller.ts

---

# 4. Role-Based Suffix Enforcement

The following suffixes must be used:

Controllers:
- <feature>-controller.ts

Services:
- <feature>-service.ts

Repositories:
- <feature>-repository.ts

Middleware:
- <name>-middleware.ts

DTOs:
- create-<feature>.dto.ts
- update-<feature>.dto.ts

Types:
- <feature>.types.ts

Interfaces:
- <feature>.interface.ts

Validators:
- <feature>-validator.ts

Tests:
- <file-name>.spec.ts
OR
- <file-name>.test.ts

Choose one convention and keep it consistent.

---

# 5. TypeScript Naming Conventions

Classes:
- PascalCase
- Must match exported class name

Example:

// user-service.ts
export class UserService {}

Interfaces:
- PascalCase
- No "I" prefix

✅ UserRepository
❌ IUserRepository

Functions:
- camelCase

Variables:
- camelCase

Constants:
- UPPER_SNAKE_CASE only for true constants

---

# 6. Import Rules

Use absolute imports via path alias:

@/* → src/*

Example:

import { UserService } from '@/modules/user/user-service'

Avoid relative deep imports:

❌ ../../../modules/user/user-service

---

# 7. Barrel File Usage

Barrel files (index.ts) are allowed only inside feature modules.

Do NOT create global barrel exports across the entire project.

---

# 8. Strict Enforcement

When generating or modifying code:

- Always follow kebab-case for files and folders.
- Always apply correct suffix based on file responsibility.
- Always place code inside a feature module.
- Never introduce layer-first structure.
- Never introduce inconsistent naming.

If existing code violates these standards, refactor to comply.

---

# Summary

Architecture Style: Feature-first modular
File Naming: kebab-case
Class Naming: PascalCase
Function Naming: camelCase
Suffix Pattern: Role-based explicit naming

Consistency is mandatory.